        label_smoothing (`float`, defaults to 0):\n    29→            The label smoothing factor. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\n    30→        loss_type (`str`, defaults to `sigmoid`):\n    31→            The type of loss to use. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\n    32→        label_pad_token_id (`int`, defaults to `-100`):\n    33→            The label pad token id. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\n    34→        padding_value (`int`, defaults to `None`):\n    35→            The padding value if it is different to the tokenizer's pad_token_id.\n    36→        truncation_mode (`str`, defaults to `keep_end`):\n    37→            The truncation mode to use, either `keep_end` or `keep_start`. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\n    38→        generate_during_eval (`bool`, defaults to `False`):\n    39→            Whether to sample and log generations during evaluation step.\n    40→        is_encoder_decoder (`Optional[bool]`, `optional`, defaults to `None`):\n    41→            If no model is provided, we need to know if the model_init returns an encoder-decoder.\n    42→        disable_dropout (`bool`, defaults to `True`):\n    43→            Whether or not to disable dropouts in `model`.\n    44→        model_init_kwargs (`Optional[Dict]`, *optional*):\n    45→            Dict of Optional kwargs to pass when instantiating the model from a string\n    46→        dataset_num_proc (`Optional[int]`, *optional*):\n    47→            The number of workers to use to tokenize the data. Defaults to None.\n    48→    \"\"\"\n    49→    \n    50→    max_length: Optional[int] = None\n    51→    max_prompt_length: Optional[int] = None\n    52→    max_completion_length: Optional[int] = None\n    53→    max_target_length: Optional[int] = None\n    54→\n    55→    beta: float = 2.0\n    56→    gamma_beta_ratio: float = 0.25\n    57→    sft_weight: float = 0.0\n    58→    label_smoothing: float = 0\n    59→    loss_type: Literal[\"sigmoid\", \"hinge\"] = \"sigmoid\"\n    60→    disable_dropout: bool = True\n    61→\n    62→    label_pad_token_id: int = -100\n    63→    padding_value: int = None\n    64→    truncation_mode: str = \"keep_end\"\n    65→    generate_during_eval: bool = False\n    66→    is_encoder_decoder: Optional[bool] = None\n    67→\n    68→    model_init_kwargs: Optional[Dict] = None\n    69→\n    70→    dataset_num_proc: Optional[int] = None\n    71→\n    72→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"uuid":"fec39f41-b334-4683-820c-6366002f7991","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:17:23.915Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3372e0e-ad10-4f76-9d08-1a9b500e91db"}
