152→\n   153→### Use our models for inference\n   154→Please refer to the [generate.py](generate.py) script for detailed instructions on loading the model with the appropriate chat template.\n   155→\n   156→## Install Requirements\n   157→\n   158→Our codebase is built upon the [alignment-handbook repo](https://github.com/huggingface/alignment-handbook). The following steps will guide you through the installation process.\n   159→\n   160→First, create a Python virtual environment using e.g. Conda:\n   161→```shell\n   162→conda create -n handbook python=3.10 && conda activate handbook\n   163→```\n   164→\n   165→Next, install PyTorch `v2.2.2`. Since this is hardware-dependent, we\n   166→direct you to the [PyTorch Installation Page](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/).\n   167→\n   168→You can then install the remaining package dependencies of [alignment-handbook](https://github.com/huggingface/alignment-handbook) as follows:\n   169→\n   170→```shell\n   171→git clone https://github.com/huggingface/alignment-handbook.git\n   172→cd ./alignment-handbook/\n   173→python -m pip install .\n   174→```\n   175→\n   176→You will also need Flash Attention 2 installed, which can be done by running:\n   177→\n   178→```shell\n   179→python -m pip install flash-attn --no-build-isolation\n   180→```\n   181→\n   182→## Training Scripts\n   183→\n   184→We provide four training config files for the four training setups reported in our paper. The training config is set for 4xH100 GPUs. You may need to adjust `num_processes` and `per_device_train_batch_size` based on your computation environment. \n   185→\n   186→* Mistral-Base:\n   187→```shell\n   188→ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/mistral-7b-base-simpo.yaml\n   189→```\n   190→* Mistral-Instruct:\n   191→```shell\n   192→ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/mistral-7b-instruct-simpo.yaml\n   193→```\n   194→* Llama3-Base:\n   195→```shell\n   196→ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/llama-3-8b-base-simpo.yaml\n   197→```\n   198→* Llama3-Instruct:\n   199→```shell\n   200→ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo.yaml\n   201→```\n   202→* Llama3-Instruct v0.2:\n   203→```shell\n   204→ACCELERATE_LOG_LEVEL=info accelerate launch --config_file accelerate_configs/deepspeed_zero3.yaml scripts/run_simpo.py training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo-v2.yaml\n   205→```\n   206→\n   207→## Evaluation\n   208→\n   209→We follow the official implementation for evaluation on AlpacaEval 2, Arena-Hard, and MT-Bench, as follows (more details can be found under [the eval directory](https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO/tree/main/eval)):\n   210→\n   211→* AlpacaEval 2: Please refer to the [AlpacaEval repo](https://github.com/tatsu-lab/alpaca_eval) for evaluation.\n   212→\n   213→* Arena-Hard: Please refer to to the [Arena-Hard-Auto repo](https://github.com/lm-sys/arena-hard-auto) for evaluation.\n   214→\n   215→* MT-Bench: Please refer to the [FastChat repo](https://github.com/lm-sys/FastChat) for evaluation.\n   216→\n   217→## Bugs or Questions?\n   218→If you have any questions related to the code or the paper, feel free to email Yu (yumeng5@virginia.edu). If you encounter any problems when using the code, or want to report a bug, feel free to open an issue! Please try to specify the problem with details so we can help you better and quicker!\n   219→\n   220→## Citation\n   221→Please cite our paper if you find the repo helpful in your work:\n   222→\n   223→```bibtex\n   224→@inproceedings{meng2024simpo,\n   225→   title={SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward},\n   226→   author={Meng, Yu and Xia, Mengzhou and Chen, Danqi},\n   227→   booktitle={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)},\n   228→   year={2024}\n   229→}\n   230→```\n   231→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"uuid":"41b46bb3-c0be-428d-8cc5-3a64a89c358f","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:17:28.821Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b61202b9-d3a0-4fb5-833e-8d052261eb06"}
